{"actor":{"id":"claude-sonnet-5","type":"agent"},"content":{"agent":"general-purpose","blocks":[{"text":"# Machinery-kind actor inventory across cledger adapters\n\n## Shared mechanism (`src/adapters/records.ts`)\n\nFour builder functions produce the four kinds. Only one accepts a caller-supplied actor type:\n\n| Builder | Kind | `actorType` | file:line |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `sessionStateDraft` | `session_state` | **hardcoded `\"system\"`**, no parameter | `records.ts:140` — `recordDraft(ctx, \"session_state\", \"system\", ...)` |\n| `activityDraft` | `activity` | **parameterized**, `actorType = \"system\"` default | `records.ts:151-158` — `function activityDraft(..., actorType = \"system\")` → `recordDraft(ctx, \"activity\", actorType, ...)` |\n| `contextInjectionDraft` | `context_injection` | **hardcoded `\"system\"`**, no parameter | `records.ts:169-182` — `recordDraft(ctx, \"context_injection\", \"system\", ...)` |\n| `fileSnapshotDraft` | `file_snapshot` | **hardcoded `\"system\"`**, no parameter | `records.ts:226-243` — `recordDraft(ctx, \"file_snapshot\", \"system\", ...)` |\n\n`recordDraft` (`records.ts:60-71`) attaches real git identity (`actor.id`/`actor.display`) only when `actorType === \"human\"`.\n\n## Per-adapter, per-kind inventory\n\n| Adapter | Kind | Source type/subtype | `actor.type` | file:line | Derived or constant? |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| claude-code | `session_state` | `mode`, `permission-mode`, `agent-setting`, `agent-name`, `ai-title`, `last-prompt`, `summary`, `relocated`, `worktree-state`, `pr-link`, `bridge-session` | `system` | `claude-code.ts:390-391` | constant |\n| claude-code | `activity` | `progress`, `queue-operation` | `system` | `claude-code.ts:394-397` (no actorType arg) | constant |\n| claude-code | `activity` | `system/${subtype}` (untyped `system` lines) | `system` | `claude-code.ts:377` | constant |\n| claude-code | `context_injection` | `attachment/${attachmentType}` | `system` | `claude-code.ts:382-387` | constant |\n| claude-code | `file_snapshot` | `file-history-snapshot`, `file-history-delta` | `system` | `claude-code.ts:345` | constant |\n| codex | `session_state` | `session_meta`, `turn_context`, `world_state` | `system` | `codex.ts:345` | constant |\n| codex | `session_state` | `event_msg/thread_settings_applied` | `system` | `codex.ts:352-354` | constant |\n| codex | `activity` | `compacted`, `inter_agent_communication_metadata` | `system` | `codex.ts:346` (no actorType arg) | constant |\n| codex | `activity` | `event_msg/${pt}` (token counts, patches, aborts, rollbacks, task/sub-agent events) | `agent` if `pt` starts with `task_`/`sub_agent`, else `system` | `codex.ts:357-358` | **derived from `pt`** (agent/system only, never human) |\n| codex | — | no `context_injection` or `file_snapshot` emitted | — | — | — |\n| opencode | `activity` | `step-start`, `step-finish`, `patch` | `agent` | `opencode.ts:457` | constant (fixed 5th arg `\"agent\"`) |\n| opencode | — | no `session_state`, `context_injection`, or `file_snapshot` emitted | — | — | — |\n| gemini-cli | `session_state` | `$set`/header metadata patch (`\"metadata\"`) | `system` | `gemini-cli.ts:584` | constant |\n| gemini-cli | `activity` | `rewind` (explicit `$rewindTo` — **user-initiated**) | `system` | `gemini-cli.ts:581-582` (no actorType arg) | constant, despite module doc explicitly stating \"the user rewound\" (`gemini-cli.ts:12,30`) |\n| gemini-cli | `activity` | `snapshot_drop` (quiet `$set.messages` truncation) | `system` | `gemini-cli.ts:581-582` | constant |\n| gemini-cli | `activity` | `notice/${type}` (textless `info`/`error`/`warning`) | `system` | `gemini-cli.ts:519` (no actorType arg) | constant |\n| gemini-cli | — | no `context_injection` or `file_snapshot` emitted | — | — | — |\n| qwen-code | `session_state` | `custom_title`, `session_source`, `parent_session`, `goal_state` | `system` | `qwen-code.ts:340` | constant |\n| qwen-code | `context_injection` | `at_command`, `agent_bootstrap`, `agent_launch_prompt` | `system` | `qwen-code.ts:343` | constant — includes `at_command`, a human-typed `@`-gesture |\n| qwen-code | `file_snapshot` | `attribution_snapshot` | `system` | `qwen-code.ts:315-321` | constant |\n| qwen-code | `file_snapshot` | other subtypes (e.g. `file_history_snapshot`) | `system` | `qwen-code.ts:337` | constant |\n| qwen-code | `activity` | fallback `system/${subtype}` (includes `slash_command` and all other unlisted subtypes) | **`human`** for `subtype === \"slash_command\"`, else `system` | `qwen-code.ts:348-354` — `HUMAN_DRIVEN_SUBTYPES.has(subtype) ? \"human\" : \"system\"`, `HUMAN_DRIVEN_SUBTYPES = new Set([\"slash_command\"])` at `qwen-code.ts:111` | **genuinely derived**, and carries real git identity via `ctx.identity` |\n\n## The \"which is attributed to human\" question\n\nAcross all five adapters and all four machinery kinds, there is exactly **one** case where a machinery-kind event gets `actor.type: \"human\"`: qwen-code's `slash_command` subtype, routed to `activity` at `qwen-code.ts:353`. Everywhere else in `session_state`, `context_injection`, and `file_snapshot` — in every adapter — the actor is unconditionally `\"system\"`, because those three builder functions in `records.ts` take no `actorType` parameter at all.\n\n## Verifying the roadmap claim\n\nREADME.md:340 says `\"activity` already carries a real actor for exactly this reason.\" This is **half true**:\n\n- **True in mechanism**: `activityDraft` is the only one of the four builders with a real `actorType` parameter, and two adapters exercise it meaningfully — qwen-code's `slash_command` → `human` (`qwen-code.ts:353`) and codex's `task_`/`sub_agent` event_msg types → `agent` (`codex.ts:357-358`).\n- **False as a general claim**: most `activity` call sites still pass no override and get the hardcoded `\"system\"` default, including two cases that are unambiguously human-driven gestures:\n  - **claude-code's `queue-operation`** (`claude-code.ts:394-397`) — the adapter